The '''Joint Base Maracaxá''' ({{lang-bl|Base Conjunta Maracaxá}}) is a military base of the [[Confederal Armed Forces]] (''Marina confederales''), located in [[Maracaju]], on the island of [[Pindorama]]. It is an amalgamation of the [[Confederal Aerospace Force|Aerospace Force]]'s [[Maracaxá Air Base]] and the [[Confederal Navy|Navy's]] [[Naval Station Maracaxá]], which were merged in 1979. Since the [[South Atlantic War]], it has undergone continuous strengthening as the northernmost base of the Confederal military. 

JB Maracaxá's [[W:Area of responsibility|area of responsibility]] (AOR) includes the [[W:Ilhas Cagarras|Cagarras Strait]], the [[Salsipuedes Sea]], and the [[W:South Atlantic Ocean|South Atlantic Ocean]]. The command's primary missions are maintaining security of the island of [[Pindorama]] and it's surroundings, [[W:Area denial weapon|area denial]] for hostile forces ([[W:Blockade|on sea]] and [[W:No-fly zone|in the air]]), and reconnaissance. It is also likely responsible for matters relating to equatorial regions, including the [[Brazil]], [[Siculia]] and [[W:West Africa|West Africa]].

